# AGENTS.md — `data/` (data layer)

Root `../AGENTS.md` applies. Human orientation: [`README.md`](README.md). These are
the hard constraints for touching data.

## Rules
- **`raw/` is immutable and read-only.** Never modify, delete, rename, reformat, or
  "clean" a file in `data/raw/`. Corrections and exclusions happen in the pipeline
  via config, so they are visible and reversible. This is the most important rule
  in the repo.
- **`interim/` and `processed/` are pipeline-owned.** Don't hand-create or hand-edit
  them — they're regenerated by `snakemake`. If one looks wrong, fix the stage.
- **Never `git add` data files.** Data is versioned by **{{ data_versioning }}**.
  Use `{{ data_versioning }} pull` / `push`. Only this README, `AGENTS.md`, and
  `.gitignore` are tracked in git here.
- **A file must have a manifest row.** The pipeline discovers inputs via
  `../metadata/` manifests; a raw file with no validated row is invisible and
  should not be relied on.

## You may
- Run `{{ data_versioning }} pull` to fetch data.
- Read from `raw/` in pipeline stages.

## You may not (without the user)
- Add, move, or delete raw files; edit manifests to point at new raw data;
  `{{ data_versioning }} push` new versions. These are human-gated provenance actions.
